-- Tests for the EU modules. Every expected value is read from the source, cited beside it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`
IMPORT `eu-ai-act-art50`
IMPORT `eu-code-of-practice`
IMPORT `test-kit`

§ `Art. 50(2) -- the provider's duty to ensure outputs are marked`

-- Art. 113: applies from 2 August 2026, not before.
#ASSERT     `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` `the generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `2 August 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` `the generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 August 2026`

-- Art. 111(4): a system placed on the market before 2 August 2026 must comply by 2 December 2026.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` `a legacy generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `2 August 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` `a legacy generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 December 2026`
#ASSERT     `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` `a legacy generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `2 December 2026`

-- 50(2), third sentence: each exception alone defeats the duty.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the colour-adjusted photo` `the editor` `EU: standard editing` `1 October 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the filtered photo` `the editor` (`EU judgements: standard editing` TRUE `, not substantial` FALSE `, falsely authentic` FALSE `, artistic` FALSE) `1 October 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the filtered photo` `the editor` (`EU judgements: standard editing` FALSE `, not substantial` TRUE `, falsely authentic` FALSE `, artistic` FALSE) `1 October 2026`
#ASSERT     `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the filtered photo` `the editor` (`EU judgements: standard editing` FALSE `, not substantial` FALSE `, falsely authentic` FALSE `, artistic` FALSE) `1 October 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is authorised for law enforcement`) `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026`

-- 50(2) reaches only the outputs of an AI system: a photo no AI system touched is not one.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `a photo nobody altered` `the generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026`

-- 50(2) reaches "synthetic audio, image, video or text content": text is in.
#ASSERT     `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `an AI-written article` `the generator` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026`

-- Adherence to the Code is irrelevant to whether the duty exists.
#ASSERT     `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `does not adhere to the Code`) `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026`

§ `Code of Practice, Measure 1.1 -- two layers, and the single-layer cases`

-- Sub-measure 1.1.1 alone (a signed manifest declaring AI, no watermark): not two layers.
#ASSERT NOT `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `the AI-generated image` `the generator`
-- Both layers.
#ASSERT     `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `the AI-generated image with a watermark` `the generator`
-- Neither layer.
#ASSERT NOT `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `the AI-generated image, stripped` `the generator`
-- Sub-measure 1.1.2 alone, on an image: not two layers.
#ASSERT NOT `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` (`content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` NOTHING `watermarked` TRUE) `the generator`
-- 1.1.1 needs a manifest that records the content is AI-generated or manipulated: a
-- camera-capture manifest does not, so a watermark beside it is still one layer.
#ASSERT NOT `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` (`content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` `the manifest of c2pa-rs-camera-capture` `watermarked` TRUE) `the generator`
-- Free-form text: a single layer under 1.1.2 suffices.
#ASSERT     `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `an AI-written article` `the generator`
-- Very short free-form text: excepted from 1.1.2, and free-form text cannot carry 1.1.1 (fork F4).
#ASSERT     `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `an AI-written caption of eight words` `the generator`
-- A closed physical product: a single layer of either kind suffices.
#ASSERT     `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `an AI image inside a closed training simulator` `the generator`
-- A provider that does not adhere to the Code: the Code says nothing about it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `does not adhere to the Code`)
        BECAUSE "the provider does not adhere to the Code of Practice, and whether its marking meets Article 50(2) is an assessment this encoding does not make"

§ `Art. 50(4) first subparagraph -- deep fakes`

#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a business publishing a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `2 August 2026` EQUALS `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
-- Art. 113.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a business publishing a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 August 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- 3(4): a personal non-professional user is not a deployer.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a private person posting a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- 3(60): it must resemble existing persons, objects, places, entities or events ...
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a business publishing an image of nothing real` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- ... and would falsely appear authentic or truthful.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a business publishing a lifelike image` (`EU judgements: standard editing` FALSE `, not substantial` FALSE `, falsely authentic` FALSE `, artistic` FALSE) `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- The artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work: limited disclosure.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a business publishing a lifelike image` (`EU judgements: standard editing` FALSE `, not substantial` FALSE `, falsely authentic` TRUE `, artistic` TRUE) `1 October 2026` EQUALS `disclosure of the existence of such generated or manipulated content, in a manner that does not hamper the display or enjoyment of the work`
-- Law enforcement.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `the AI-generated image` `a police unit publishing a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- 3(60): "AI-generated or manipulated": an untouched camera capture is not a deep fake.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `a photo nobody altered` `a business publishing a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- 3(60) reaches "image, audio or video content": text is never a deep fake.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on a deep fake` `an AI-written article` `a business publishing a lifelike image` `EU: a substantive, lifelike output` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`

§ `Art. 50(4) second subparagraph -- text published to inform the public`

#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `an AI-written article` `a news site publishing unreviewed AI text` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
-- Human review or editorial control AND editorial responsibility: both needed for the exception.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `an AI-written article` `a newspaper publishing edited AI text` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `an AI-written article` `a news site publishing reviewed AI text nobody is responsible for` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
-- Not published to inform the public on matters of public interest.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `an AI-written article` `a business publishing an image of nothing real` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- Art. 113.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `an AI-written article` `a news site publishing unreviewed AI text` `1 August 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
-- An image is not text.
#ASSERT `Article 50(4) on public-interest text` `the AI-generated image` `a news site publishing unreviewed AI text` `1 October 2026` EQUALS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
